				1486,
				5
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Modularize DNS and TLS command modules into sub-files\n\nSplit the monolithic `DnsCommands.rs` and `TlsCommands.rs` files into a directory structure of individual sub-modules, adhering to the project's strict PascalCase naming conventions. Each command handler, DTO, and utility now resides in its own file (e.g., `DnsServerInfo`, `ZoneInfo`, `tls_check_cert_status`), reducing file size and improving maintainability.\n\nConcurrently, updated `LoggingPlugin.rs` to align helper method calls with the new `::Fn()` explicit qualification pattern and refined `PostHogPlugin.rs` documentation to include the new `CaptureHandler` and `HydrateRuntimeEnvironment` modules. Removed extensive inline documentation in favor of concise module-level comments, as the new file structure provides natural separation of concerns.\n\nThis refactoring prepares the codebase for easier registration in `Entry.rs` and aligns with the architectural shift towards fine-grained modularity within the `Binary/Build` layer.",
			"SHA": "3ab7ccaa338e67a0aeb0e24a528cb57b4112782a"
		},
