			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Update registration imports to use explicit namespace qualification\n\nAlign the import statements in `Source/Binary/Register/AdvancedFeaturesRegister.rs` and `Source/Binary/Register/StatusReporterRegister.rs` with the project's strict Rust formatting conventions. The initialization functions for the IPC subsystems are now explicitly qualified within their respective module namespaces (`IPC::AdvancedFeatures::InitializeAdvancedFeatures` and `IPC::StatusReporter::InitializeStatusReporter`).\n\nThis change ensures consistency with recent modularization efforts where function names are scoped to their logical module containers, improving type clarity and preventing potential symbol collisions in the large Mountain codebase. No functional logic is altered; this is a pure refactoring to maintain codebase hygiene.",
